module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SymmetricAlgebraConstruction.Scheme
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeVeryAmpleTwist.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.Hom

/-!
# The canonical graded-algebra map `Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜`

Stacks Tags 07ZR and 0B3U both begin with "the morphism associated to the graded
`𝒪_S`-algebra map `Sym*_{𝒪_S}(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜`". This file constructs that map: for every sheaf-level
graded algebra `𝒜` in the sense of Situation 01NN there is a homomorphism of graded algebras
`Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜` restricting to the identity on the degree-one piece, and it is the unique such.

It is the universal property of the symmetric algebra applied to the degree-one generator
`𝟙 : 𝒜_1 ⟶ 𝒜_1`, whose image commutes pairwise because the multiplication of a
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra` is commutative by one of its
fields. The universal property itself is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.isSymmetricAlgebra_symmetricAlgebra`, over an arbitrary base.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra.asGradedAlgebra`: the
  sheaf-level graded algebra data of Situation 01NN, read as a `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra`.
  This is the inverse of
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SheafSymmetricAlgebra.toSheafGradedAlgebra`, and it carries the data
  across unchanged.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.SheafGradedAlgebraHom.ofUnitalHom`: a unital
  homomorphism of the underlying sheaves of graded algebras, read as a homomorphism of
  sheaf-level graded algebra data.
* `Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymHom`: **the canonical map `Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜`.**

## Main results

* `Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.symmetricAlgebraGen_comp_canonicalSymHom_app_one`: it is the
  identity on the degree-one piece, which is the property that pins it down.
* `Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymHom_unique`: uniqueness.

## Implementation notes

**The two spellings of the data are definitionally equal.** `SheafGradedAlgebra` records the
multiplication over `S.Opens` and `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra` over `(S.Opens)ᵒᵖ`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` is a `def` with its own `Category` instance; but the
underlying `Hom`, identity and composition are those of `SheafOfModules`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.Hom.app` is the given morphism's component at `op U`. So every
field below is the given field read at `op U`, with no coercion written — the same device as in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SheafSymmetricAlgebra.Bridge`.

**Why the generator is the identity.** The universal property produces a unital homomorphism out
of `Sym(M)` from a degree-one generator `M ⟶ B_1`. Taking `M = 𝒜_1` and `B = 𝒜` the generator
wanted is the identity, and `PairwiseCommutes` of it is commutativity of `𝒜` in degree `(1, 1)`,
where the two sides already live in the same piece, so the `HEq` of the field is an `Eq`.

**No tag is claimed.** The map constructed here is an input of Tags 07ZR and 0B3U, not a statement
of either. What those tags additionally need of it is that `Sym^d(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜_d` be surjective for
`d ≥ 1` when `𝒜` is generated by `𝒜_1` over `𝒜_0`, which is not proved here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B3U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B3U)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (A : SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} S)

/-- **Sheaf-level graded algebra data, read as a sheaf of graded algebras.** The inverse of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SheafSymmetricAlgebra.toSheafGradedAlgebra`: the multiplication at
`U : (S.Opens)ᵒᵖ` is the given multiplication at `U.unop`, and the global unit is the given
restriction-compatible family. The three further requirements of `SheafGradedAlgebra` —
commutativity, vanishing in negative degrees, quasi-coherence — are simply forgotten. -/
public def asGradedAlgebra : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u} S.ringCatSheaf where
  piece n := A.piece n
  mul i j :=
    { app U := (A.mul i j).app U.unop
      map_smul_left U r x y := (A.mul i j).map_smul_left U.unop r x y
      map_smul_right U r x y := (A.mul i j).map_smul_right U.unop r x y
      naturality f x y := (A.mul i j).naturality (leOfHom f.unop) x y }
  one := PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk (fun U => A.one U.unop)
    fun {_ _} f => A.one_res (leOfHom f.unop)
  mul_assoc i j k U a b c := A.mul_assoc i j k U.unop a b c
  one_mul i U a := A.one_mul i U.unop a
  mul_one i U a := A.mul_one i U.unop a

/-- The pieces are carried across unchanged. -/
public theorem asGradedAlgebra_piece (n : ℤ) : (asGradedAlgebra A).piece n = A.piece n := rfl

/-- The multiplication is carried across unchanged. -/
public theorem asGradedAlgebra_mul_app (i j : ℤ) (U : S.Opens) :
    ((asGradedAlgebra A).mul i j).app (op U) = (A.mul i j).app U := rfl

/-- The unit is carried across unchanged. -/
public theorem asGradedAlgebra_one_eval (U : S.Opens) :
    (asGradedAlgebra A).one.eval (op U) = A.one U := rfl

/-- **The identity is a pairwise-commuting degree-one generator**, because the multiplication of
sheaf-level graded algebra data is commutative. In degree `(1, 1)` the two sides of the
commutativity field live in the same homogeneous piece, so its `HEq` is an `Eq`. -/
public theorem pairwiseCommutes_id :
    SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.PairwiseCommutes
      (A := asGradedAlgebra A) (𝟙 (A.piece 1)) :=
  fun U s u => eq_of_heq (A.mul_comm 1 1 U.unop s u)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.SheafGradedAlgebraHom

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} {A B : SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} S}

/-- **A unital homomorphism of the underlying sheaves of graded algebras, read as a homomorphism
of sheaf-level graded algebra data.** Each law is the given law at `op U`. -/
public def ofUnitalHom
    (g : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom A.asGradedAlgebra B.asGradedAlgebra) :
    SheafGradedAlgebraHom A B where
  app n := g.app n
  app_mul i j U a b := g.map_mul i j (op U) a b
  app_one U := g.map_one (op U)

/-- The homogeneous components of `ofUnitalHom g` are those of `g`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem ofUnitalHom_app
    (g : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom A.asGradedAlgebra B.asGradedAlgebra) (n : ℤ) :
    (ofUnitalHom g).app n = g.app n := rfl

/-- The converse reading: a homomorphism of sheaf-level graded algebra data is a unital
homomorphism of the underlying sheaves of graded algebras. -/
public def toUnitalHom (ψ : SheafGradedAlgebraHom A B) :
    SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom A.asGradedAlgebra B.asGradedAlgebra where
  app n := ψ.app n
  map_mul i j U a b := ψ.app_mul i j U.unop a b
  map_one U := ψ.app_one U.unop

/-- The homogeneous components of `toUnitalHom ψ` are those of `ψ`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem toUnitalHom_app (ψ : SheafGradedAlgebraHom A B) (n : ℤ) :
    (toUnitalHom ψ).app n = ψ.app n := rfl

/-- Two homomorphisms of sheaf-level graded algebra data agree as soon as all their homogeneous
components do. -/
@[ext]
public theorem ext {ψ χ : SheafGradedAlgebraHom A B} (h : ∀ n, ψ.app n = χ.app n) : ψ = χ := by
  cases ψ; cases χ; congr; funext n; exact h n

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.SheafGradedAlgebraHom

namespace Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (A : SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} S)

/-- **The canonical map `Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜`**, as a unital homomorphism of the underlying sheaves of
graded algebras: the extension of the identity generator `𝒜_1 ⟶ 𝒜_1` along the universal
property of the symmetric algebra of `𝒜_1`. -/
def canonicalSymUnitalHom :
    SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom (Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebra S (A.piece 1))
      A.asGradedAlgebra :=
  ((Scheme.Modules.isSymmetricAlgebra_symmetricAlgebra S (A.piece 1)).2 A.asGradedAlgebra
    (𝟙 (A.piece 1)) (SheafGradedAlgebra.pairwiseCommutes_id A)).choose

/-- The canonical map restricts to the identity on the degree-one piece, and is the only unital
homomorphism which does. -/
private theorem canonicalSymUnitalHom_spec :
    Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraGen S (A.piece 1) ≫ (canonicalSymUnitalHom A).app 1 =
      𝟙 (A.piece 1) ∧
    ∀ g : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom (Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebra S (A.piece 1))
      A.asGradedAlgebra,
      Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraGen S (A.piece 1) ≫ g.app 1 = 𝟙 (A.piece 1) →
        g = canonicalSymUnitalHom A :=
  ((Scheme.Modules.isSymmetricAlgebra_symmetricAlgebra S (A.piece 1)).2 A.asGradedAlgebra
    (𝟙 (A.piece 1)) (SheafGradedAlgebra.pairwiseCommutes_id A)).choose_spec

/-- The canonical map restricts to the identity on the degree-one piece. -/
theorem symmetricAlgebraGen_comp_canonicalSymUnitalHom_app_one :
    Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraGen S (A.piece 1) ≫ (canonicalSymUnitalHom A).app 1 =
      𝟙 (A.piece 1) :=
  (canonicalSymUnitalHom_spec A).1

/-- It is the only unital homomorphism which does. -/
theorem canonicalSymUnitalHom_unique
    (g : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom (Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebra S (A.piece 1))
      A.asGradedAlgebra)
    (hg : Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraGen S (A.piece 1) ≫ g.app 1 = 𝟙 (A.piece 1)) :
    g = canonicalSymUnitalHom A :=
  (canonicalSymUnitalHom_spec A).2 g hg

/-- **The canonical graded-algebra map `Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜`**, in the shape Stacks Tags 07ZR and 0B3U
consume: a `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.SheafGradedAlgebraHom` out of
`Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.symAlgebra` of the degree-one piece.

This is the map the source means by `Sym*_{𝒪_S}(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜`. -/
def canonicalSymHom : SheafGradedAlgebraHom (symAlgebra (A.piece 1)) A :=
  SheafGradedAlgebraHom.ofUnitalHom (canonicalSymUnitalHom A)

/-- The homogeneous components of `canonicalSymHom A` are those of `canonicalSymUnitalHom A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem canonicalSymHom_app (n : ℤ) :
    (canonicalSymHom A).app n = (canonicalSymUnitalHom A).app n := rfl

/-- **The canonical map is the identity on the degree-one piece**, which is what pins it down. -/
theorem symmetricAlgebraGen_comp_canonicalSymHom_app_one :
    Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraGen S (A.piece 1) ≫ (canonicalSymHom A).app 1 =
      𝟙 (A.piece 1) :=
  symmetricAlgebraGen_comp_canonicalSymUnitalHom_app_one A

/-- **Uniqueness of the canonical map**: a homomorphism of graded algebras out of `Sym(𝒜_1)` which
is the identity on the degree-one piece is the canonical one. -/
theorem canonicalSymHom_unique (ψ : SheafGradedAlgebraHom (symAlgebra (A.piece 1)) A)
    (hψ : Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraGen S (A.piece 1) ≫ ψ.app 1 = 𝟙 (A.piece 1)) :
    ψ = canonicalSymHom A :=
  SheafGradedAlgebraHom.ext fun n =>
    congrArg (fun g : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom
        (Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebra S (A.piece 1)) A.asGradedAlgebra => g.app n)
      (canonicalSymUnitalHom_unique A (SheafGradedAlgebraHom.toUnitalHom ψ) hψ)

end Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple

end
